  "habitat": "Singly or in pairs in hilly country and grassland. It perches on roadside posts, hovers 5–20 m up, and roosts on cliffs or in trees.",
  "summary": "A common resident. Grey head, rufous upperwings and underparts, and a grey upper tail. The male’s tail has a single bar. The female’s tail is well barred, and she may lack the grey head. Some females look like the immature, with the head the same colour as the rest of the plumage and heavy dark-brown streaking. Newman does not describe the voice. The Kemp code VB was left unchanged.",
